  "body": "## What happens\r\n\r\nThe solidcore STEP path (#917, PR B on `issue/917-solidcore-step`) meshes the four-turn thread flank fixture with too many facets.\r\n\r\nThe test is `crates/app/tests/import_step_thread.rs`, `a_four_turn_thread_flank_meshes_at_full_fidelity_in_a_bounded_count`.\r\n\r\n| Reading | Main (old reader, #1602 division) | solidcore path |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Facets | under 5000 (the pin passes on main) | 391338 |\r\n| Chord | 5e-3 mm | 5e-3 mm requested, replanned at 2.5e-3 mm |\r\n| Debug test time | not measured | 93 s |\r\n\r\nThe import note is: `STEP sheet #418: replanned at 2.5e-3 mm chord to meet the requested 5e-3 mm measured tolerance`.\r\n\r\n## Cause\r\n\r\nAt the pinned rev, solidcore-tess plans the long, thin helicoid strip isotropically. The plan at a 5 um chord measures over the tolerance. The seam then replans at half the chord (`PLAN_MARGIN`), and the count goes up again. Our seam (`crates/kernel/src/machining_mesh.rs`, `planned`) can only pick the chord. It cannot pick the shape of the division.\r\n\r\n## Options\r\n\r\n1. An anisotropic plan upstream in solidcore-tess: divide along the strip by the curvature of each direction.\r\n2. A division hint through our seam: pass a per-face step in u and v to the planner, if solidcore-tess gets an API for it.\r\n\r\n## Acceptance\r\n\r\nThe pin `facets.len() < 5_000` in the test above passes, with the other asserts of the test (chord not reduced, longest edge, area, axial gap). Until then, the test has the known-fail marker with this issue number.\r\n\r\nRefs #917\r\n\r\n\r\n",
